  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 configs (config_001: 0.725, config_003: 0.721, config_015: 0.713) all use multimodal + multiprofile + transformer aggregation, and scvi_n200 clearly outperforms scgpt (0.725 vs 0.520). The one major untested variable in this best-performing family is the RNA encoder: we have not yet tested pca_n2000 paired with imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. This experiment (config_011) directly tests whether a simpler PCA projection can match or exceed the learned scvi representation in the full multimodal pipeline. If pca_n2000 performs comparably, it would be a cheaper alternative; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around config_001. Expected relative cost: low (~2–3 GPU hours), since PCA encoding is substantially lighter than scvi, making this a cost-efficient probe of a critical design axis with 4 experiments still remaining."
